From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: the rest of Windows 7's headers with the right item part

Purpose: draw the header area after the last item as Windows 7 does.
Windows behavior: Windows 7 SP1 draws it with HP_HEADERITEMRIGHT; Aero's
Explorer::Header does not define the part, so the class's image is used
(a divider next to the last item, a white edge, the item gradient
starting a row higher).
Wine before: 0105 drew a mirrored HP_HEADERITEM there, which was two
rows and the divider one or two levels off.
Change: draw HP_HEADERITEMRIGHT, normal state, in the Windows 7 shell.
Evidence: tests/theme-part-pixels.c draws the part identically on
Windows 7 and in Wine; w7cmp.exe's list view header after the change is
identical to Windows 7 apart from the known glyph differences.
Scope: the Windows 7 shell (COMCTL32_IsWin7Shell), comctl32 v6.
---
 dlls/comctl32/header.c | 18 ++++--------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/comctl32/header.c b/dlls/comctl32/header.c
index 9ff2d01..96d953f 100644
--- a/dlls/comctl32/header.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/header.c
@@ -629,22 +629,12 @@ static void HEADER_DrawRestBackground(HEADER_INFO *infoPtr, HDC hdc, RECT *rect)
 #if __WINE_COMCTL32_VERSION == 6
     HTHEME theme = GetWindowTheme(infoPtr->hwndSelf);
 
+    /* Windows 7 SP1 draws the rest with the right item part, which Aero's
+     * Explorer::Header leaves to the class's image (its divider next to the
+     * last item), seen with tests/theme-part-pixels.c */
     if (theme && COMCTL32_IsWin7Shell())
     {
-        /* Windows 7 SP1 draws the rest as an item seen in a mirror: its
-         * divider next to the last item, its other edge beyond the header */
-        int width = rect->right - rect->left, height = rect->bottom - rect->top;
-        RECT r = {0, 0, width + 2, height};
-        HDC mem = CreateCompatibleDC(hdc);
-        HBITMAP bitmap = CreateCompatibleBitmap(hdc, width + 2, height);
-        HBITMAP old = SelectObject(mem, bitmap);
-
-        FillRect(mem, &r, GetSysColorBrush(COLOR_WINDOW));
-        DrawThemeBackground(theme, mem, HP_HEADERITEM, HIS_NORMAL, &r, NULL);
-        StretchBlt(hdc, rect->left + width - 1, rect->top, -width, height, mem, 2, 0, width, height, SRCCOPY);
-        SelectObject(mem, old);
-        DeleteObject(bitmap);
-        DeleteDC(mem);
+        DrawThemeBackground(theme, hdc, HP_HEADERITEMRIGHT, HIRS_NORMAL, rect, NULL);
         return;
     }
     if (theme)
